❓Question:
Given an integer array nums, create a new array ans of length 2n. The new array should contain the original array twice consecutively.

For example:
Input:  [1, 2, 1]
Output: [1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1]

✅Approach:
Create a new array with double the size of nums. Use a loop to place each element at its original index and again at i + nums.length.

Code:
class Solution {
    public int[] getConcatenation(int[] nums) {
        int[] ans = new int[nums.length * 2];
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            ans[i] = nums[i];
            ans[i + nums.length] = nums[i];
        }
        return ans;
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(n)
